<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>AI Settings — SharifTech Admin</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/main.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/admin.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="admin-shell">
    <%- include('../partials/sidebar') %>
    <main class="admin-main">
      <div class="admin-topbar"><h1>AI Settings</h1></div>
      <div class="admin-content" style="max-width:600px;">

        <form method="POST" action="/admin/ai/settings">
          <div class="panel">
            <h2>Provider</h2>
            <div class="field">
              <label>AI Provider</label>
              <select name="ai_provider">
                <option value="gemini" <%= provider === 'gemini' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Google Gemini</option>
              </select>
              <div class="hint">Only Gemini is currently supported. Additional providers can be added later without changing how content generation works elsewhere in the app.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="field">
              <label>Model</label>
              <input type="text" name="ai_model" value="<%= model %>">
              <div class="hint">
                Default: <code>gemini-1.5-flash</code> — the most generous free-tier limits (15 requests/min, 1,500/day) as of when this was set up. Only change this if you know what you're doing; an invalid model name will cause every generation to fail.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="panel" style="background:#eaf0ff;border-color:#c7d8ff;">
            <h2>API Key</h2>
            <p style="font-size:0.85rem;">
              The Gemini API key is stored in your server's <code>.env</code> file as <code>GEMINI_API_KEY</code> — not here, since this settings page is readable from the admin dashboard and a secret key should never be stored or displayed there.
            </p>
          </div>

          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save Settings</button>
        </form>

      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
